Jon Favreau's reimagining of the jungle  book has been a huge success and has  pulled the punters in like bears too  honey however this is not the only  adaptation of the classic story that is  to be released in the next couple of  years I'm Simon and this is your  entertainment news update Warner  Brothers are also making a version of  the jungle book but are pushed back the  release date the studio is now looking  at other ways to set it apart from its  smash-hit rival it has now been reported  that gravity and harry potter and the  prisoner of azkaban director alfonso  quran is coming on board to lend a hand  according to Deadline the oscar-winning  filmmaker is joining the project to give  notes and to see how the film can be  improved the site reports that the  studio is sensitive to the suggestion  that Curran is taking over the project  from director Andy Serkis and stresses  that he is purely there as a friend to  the studio production on the film has  already wrapped but earlier this month  Warner made the decision to move the  film back an entire year from its  initial release date on October 2017 to  October 2018 the film originally had the  title jungle book origins but is now  simply called Jungle Book circus took to  Facebook to comment on the decision to  shift the release date stating that he  was absolutely thrilled to have another  year to work on the movie the ambition  for this project is huge he said what we  are attempting is an unprecedented level  of psychological and emotional nuance in  morphing the phenomenal performances of  our cast into the facial expressions of  our animals so every minute more that we  have to evolve the technological  pipeline will make all the difference  the evidence is there already and it's  off the chain exciting so hang on in  there this is truly next-generation  storytelling jungle book has a course  that includes Christian Bale Benedict  Cumberbatch Cate Blanchett and Naomie  Harris it is currently set to be 